    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>Colour</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>nm</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Li</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>Crimson</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>red</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>670</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Na</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>Yellow</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>589</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Rb</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>Red</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>violet</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>780</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Cs</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>Blue</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>455</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Range of visible region: 390 nm &ndash; 760 nm</p><p>VIBGYOR</p><p>Violet &ndash; Red</p><p>LiCl Crimson Red</p><p>NaCl Golden yellow</p><p>RbCl Violet</p><p>CsCl Blue</p><p>So, LiCl which is crimson have wavelengths close to red in the spectrum of visible region which is as per given data.</p>",
